{"name":"Périgord Truffle","hex":"#524a46","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"truffle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various edible fungi, of the genus Tuber, that grow in the soil in southern Europe; the earthnut.","Ellipsis of chocolate truffle (“creamy chocolate confection, in the form of a ball, covered with cocoa powder”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/truffle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tuber melanosporum","blocks":[{"text":"Tuber melanosporum, commonly called black truffle, Périgord truffle or French black truffle, is a species of truffle native to Southern Europe. It is one of the most expensive edible fungi in the world. In 2013, the truffle cost between 1,000 and 2,000 euros per kilogram."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Truffe_nature.JPG/330px-Truffe_nature.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tuber_melanosporum","wikidata":"Q1093314"},{"title":"Périgord","blocks":[{"text":"Périgord is a natural region and former province of France, which corresponds roughly to the current Dordogne department, now forming the northern part of the administrative region of Nouvelle-Aquitaine. It is divided into four areas called the Périgord Noir (Black), named so for the truffles that can be found there, the Périgord Blanc (White), for chalk cliffs and quarries, the Périgord Vert (Green), for forests and forestry, and the Périgord Pourpre (Purple), for wine and viticulture. The geography and natural resources of Périgord make it a region rich in history and wildlife, and the newly created Parc Naturel Régional Périgord-Limousin aims to conserve it as such."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Dordogne_2.jpg/330px-Dordogne_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/P%C3%A9rigord","wikidata":"Q850620"},{"title":"Truffle","blocks":[{"text":"A truffle is the fruiting body of a subterranean ascomycete fungus, one of the species of the genus Tuber. More than one hundred other genera of fungi are classified as truffles including Geopora, Peziza, Choiromyces, and Leucangium. These genera belong to the class Pezizomycetes and the Pezizales order. Several truffle-like basidiomycetes are excluded from Pezizales, including Rhizopogon and Glomus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Truffe_noire_du_P%C3%A9rigord.jpg/330px-Truffe_noire_du_P%C3%A9rigord.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Truffle","wikidata":"Q2690965"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Truffi%C3%A8re_des_Gr%C3%A8zes_01.jpg/500px-Truffi%C3%A8re_des_Gr%C3%A8zes_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Truffi%C3%A8re_des_Gr%C3%A8zes_01.jpg/500px-Truffi%C3%A8re_des_Gr%C3%A8zes_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Black truffle, cut","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATruffi%C3%A8re_des_Gr%C3%A8zes_01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Beaumont_-_truffi%C3%A8res.jpg/500px-Beaumont_-_truffi%C3%A8res.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Beaumont_-_truffi%C3%A8res.jpg/1280px-Beaumont_-_truffi%C3%A8res.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Beaumont_-_truffi%C3%A8res.jpg/500px-Beaumont_-_truffi%C3%A8res.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Black truffles suppress the growth of plants around their symbiont, creating the impression of a b